## How Much Do Gel Nails Cost?

Budget gel and premium gel are not the same conversation. <strong>How much do gel nails cost</strong>? At the lower end, around $30 to $45, covering a standard application on short to medium natural nails. Premium gel, applied at boutique studios using higher-grade brands and more prep time, runs $50 to $80 and sometimes higher in major cities.

The price difference isn't really about the polish bottle. Gel costs salons only a few dollars more per bottle than regular lacquer. What you're paying for is the curing process, the extra ten to fifteen minutes under a UV or LED lamp, and the soak-off removal gel requires when it's time for a change. None of that is optional, and none of it is something a budget salon can skip without compromising the finish.

One Reddit comment puts the real question plainly: is it normal for gel to cost that much more than regular? Yes. Gel needs a base coat, colour, and top coat, each cured separately, plus a removal process regular polish never requires. That's roughly double the labour time of a basic manicure, and the price reflects it.

Gel lasts two to three weeks without chipping, against five to seven days for regular polish. Stretched across a month, gel often works out cheaper per day worn, even though the upfront number looks higher. For the full breakdown of gel pricing by region and salon tier, see <a href='/blog/nail-costs/gel-nails-cost'>gel nails cost</a>.

Watch for removal fees if you're switching products. Most salons charge $10 to $15 separately for removing an old gel or acrylic set before applying a new one, and that fee rarely appears on the headline price.

