## How Much Do Acrylic Nails Cost?

A full acrylic set costs more than gel, and the reason has nothing to do with marketing. Acrylics are built, not painted on. Are acrylic nails more expensive than gel? Yes, consistently. A full set runs $45 to $110 in 2026, against $30 to $80 for standard gel, because the technician is sculpting an entirely new nail structure rather than coating an existing one.

That sculpting process uses a liquid monomer and a powder polymer, mixed and applied bead by bead over a tip or form, then shaped, filed, and buffed before any colour goes on. It takes longer than gel, often forty-five minutes to over an hour for a full set, and the product costs more per appointment than gel polish does.

Length and shape move the price more than anything else here. Short, squared acrylics on natural-length nails sit at the lower end. Long stiletto or coffin shapes, needing extra product and far more shaping time, push toward $90 to $110 or beyond, especially with a design added.

A lot of cost content online is genuinely running outdated numbers, the kind behind the question "are acrylics still $60 like in 2019?" $60 was a reasonable mid-range price back then. In 2026, $60 sits at the lower-middle of the range, and major metro salons have moved well past it. For the complete breakdown including fill pricing and shape comparisons, see <a href='/blog/nail-costs/acrylic-nails-cost'>acrylic nails cost</a>.

