## How Much Does a Manicure Cost?

What is the average price of a manicure in the US right now? A basic manicure, with shaping, cuticle care, and regular polish, runs $15 to $50 depending on salon tier and city. That range hasn't shifted dramatically from previous years, but it has crept upward at the bottom end as overhead rises across the industry.

This is the service every other nail treatment gets compared against. A basic manicure includes nail trimming, shaping, cuticle work, a hand soak, and polish. It does not include gel curing, acrylic building, or any spa elements. Those sit one tier up.

What you'll pay depends heavily on where you sit on a spectrum readers have described accurately online: pedicures between $25 and $35, manicures between $15 and $35. That's broadly still right for a basic service at a standard salon. Where the number shifts is location. Major metro salons routinely start manicures at $35 to $40 and climb from there, while suburban and rural salons can still offer a basic manicure under $20.

A French manicure typically adds $5 to $15 for the precision of the tip work. A spa manicure, folding in exfoliation, a hand massage, and a hydrating mask, sits at $40 to $70. For the full price ladder across every manicure type, see <a href='/blog/nail-costs/manicure-cost'>how much does a manicure cost</a>.

