## How Much Does a Pedicure Cost?

Most people assume a pedicure costs roughly what a manicure does. It usually costs slightly more, because pedicures take longer and involve more physical work. How much does a pedicure typically cost at a nail salon? A basic pedicure runs $25 to $50, with deluxe or spa versions climbing to $50 to $90.

That gap between basic and spa is wider than for manicures, mostly because pedicure upgrades add real time. A basic pedicure covers a foot soak, trimming and shaping, cuticle care, light callus treatment, and polish. A spa upgrade adds extended massage, paraffin treatment, and exfoliating scrubs, each adding ten to twenty minutes of work.

Gel pedicures, for the longer wear, typically add $10 to $20 over a basic pedicure, landing around $40 to $65. The added cost mirrors gel manicure pricing logic: curing time and a soak-off removal process regular polish skips entirely.

One detail that surprises first-time visitors: pedicures last longer than manicures before needing a refresh, four to six weeks against two to three. Even at a slightly higher price per visit, that spacing often makes pedicures cheaper over a year than the equivalent manicure habit. See <a href='/blog/nail-costs/pedicure-cost'>how much does a pedicure cost</a> for every tier in detail.

