## How Much Do Nail Fills Cost?

A gel fill is a maintenance appointment where the technician applies fresh product to the regrowth area only, avoiding a full removal and reapplication. It is the single best way to stretch your nail budget, and most people who skip it are paying more than they need to. How much do nail fills cost? Fills typically run $25 to $45, considerably less than a full new set.

The logic here is straightforward. A full set, gel or acrylic, involves building or applying product across the entire nail. A fill only addresses the gap that's grown out near the cuticle, which takes less product and less time. Most nail techs price fills at 60 to 70 percent of the cost of a full set.

This is also where the annual cost conversation gets real. "<strong>fills every 3 weeks at $30 each, that's $520 a year just for maintenance</strong>" is a comment pulled almost word for word from real budgeting threads online, and the maths checks out. Seventeen fills a year at $30 lands at $510. Add a full new set once or twice annually and the real number creeps toward $600 to $700, a figure most pricing guides never show you because they only quote the price of one visit.

Skipping fills in favour of letting a set grow out and then removing it entirely is almost always the more expensive path, since full removal and reapplication costs more per session than a fill does. If a deeper dive into fill pricing and frequency is useful, see <a href='/blog/nail-costs/nail-fills-cost'>nail fills cost</a> for the complete breakdown.

