## How Much Does BIAB Cost?

BIAB (Builder in a Bottle) is a structured gel overlay applied to the natural nail and cured under LED light. It is the dominant nail service in UK and Australian salons, and its popularity in the US is climbing fast in 2026. How much does BIAB cost in the UK? Expect to pay £35 to £60 for a full BIAB application, roughly equivalent to $45 to $75 once converted.

BIAB sits in an interesting middle ground between gel polish and acrylic. It strengthens and slightly extends the natural nail without building a full sculpted tip, which makes it gentler on nail health than acrylic while lasting noticeably longer than standard gel, often three to four weeks rather than two.

That extra durability is exactly why the price sits where it does. You're paying for a product that needs fewer repeat visits, not for a more complicated application process. In the US, where BIAB is offered at fewer salons, prices skew slightly higher, often $50 to $85, partly because demand is outpacing supply at salons trained in the technique.

Removal matters here more than with regular gel, since BIAB's stronger bond means professional removal is worth the extra $10 to $20 it usually costs, rather than risking nail damage with an at-home soak-off. Our deeper guide on <a href='/blog/biab-cost/biab-cost-guide'>how much does BIAB cost</a> covers regional pricing and what to ask for at your first appointment.

