## How Much Does Dip Powder Cost?

What's the price difference between dip powder and gel nails? Dip powder typically runs $40 to $65 for a full set, sitting close to gel pricing but occasionally edging slightly higher depending on the salon and the number of dip layers applied.

Dip powder nails use a resin-and-powder bonding system instead of monomer liquid, creating a hard finish that falls between gel and acrylic in flexibility. Each nail is dipped into coloured powder several times, sealed, and buffed, a process that takes roughly the same time as a gel application but uses a different product category entirely.

"<strong>I pay $50 for a dip and it takes 45 minutes, is that right</strong>?" Yes, squarely within range. Forty-five minutes is a typical appointment length, and $50 sits comfortably in the middle of the national price band for a standard dip set without added length or art.

Dip's main selling point against gel is durability without UV exposure, since it air-dries rather than curing under a lamp. That makes it attractive to clients who want gel-like longevity, generally two to four weeks, without the lamp time. The trade-off is removal, which requires more soaking than gel and should be done professionally rather than picked off. The full pricing and removal guide lives at <a href='/blog/nail-costs/dip-powder-cost'>dip powder cost</a>.

