## How Much Do Nails Cost in the UK, Australia, and Canada?

A US guide is useless to a UK reader, and vice versa, which is exactly why every major nail pricing post online covers exactly one country. How much do nails cost in the UK versus the US? In raw currency terms, UK prices in pounds track close to US prices in dollars for equivalent services, which means the real cost, once converted, runs noticeably higher in the UK due to the stronger pound.

A basic manicure in the UK runs £18 to £40, against $15 to $50 in the US. Gel manicures sit around £30 to £50 in the UK compared with $30 to $80 in the US, and BIAB, which barely registers as a US service category, dominates UK salon menus at £35 to £60.

Australia runs higher across nearly every category once converted to local currency. A basic manicure costs A$30 to $50, gel sits at A$55 to $85, and acrylics land between A$40 and $70 for standard length, climbing to A$150 or more for extensions with detailed art. Tipping in Australia is genuinely optional, with rounding up the more common gesture than a fixed percentage.

Canada sits closest to US pricing of the four markets, with a basic manicure at $20 to $40 CAD and gel running $40 to $80 CAD depending heavily on city. Vancouver and Toronto sit at the top of that range, Montreal and smaller cities toward the bottom. Tipping in Canada mirrors the US closely, at 15 to 20 percent, and is considered standard rather than optional.

What no other guide currently covers is that US pricing itself varies as much within the country as it does between countries. State-level data shows the gap between, say, a rural Midwest salon and a Manhattan salon can be wider than the gap between the US national average and the UK national average. If state-by-state US pricing is what you need, the full table lives at <a href='/blog/nail-costs/nail-salon-cost-by-state'>nail salon cost by state</a>, and our most-cited source for that state data comes from <a href='https://www.styleseat.com/blog/how-much-nails-cost'>StyleSeat US nail price data</a>.

