## The Real Number to Walk In With

Every price in this guide is a starting point, not a ceiling. The salon down the street might quote less than the ranges above, and a boutique studio in a major city might quote considerably more, and both can be entirely fair prices for what they're delivering. What matters isn't memorising a single number. It's knowing which service you're booking, what it should cost given your location, and which extras are likely to land on the bill that the headline price never mentioned.

The reader who walked in expecting $35 and walked out $85 lighter wasn't overcharged. She was under-informed. Removal fees, length surcharges, and tips are not hidden costs in any dishonest sense, they're simply costs that rarely make it onto a salon's website. Now they're on yours.

Budget for the year, not the visit. Whatever service you choose, multiply it by how often you'll actually book it, add the tip, and that number, not the one on the menu, is the real cost of having great nails.
